A1. What do many girls fish for? ~ CATCH
A6. Name a promising place. ~ ALTAR
A10. Name a beastly place to live. ~ LAIR
A11. What is the most harmonious of wind instruments? ~ ORGAN
A14. What is a peasant called in India? ~ RYOT
A16. What is a favorite masculine nickname in N. Y.? ~ AL
A17. What maiden was changed into a white heifer? ~ IO
A19. What is a name for something of little value—a scrap, or refuse? ~ ORT
A20. What little word did Hamlet soliloquize over? ~ BE
A21. Name a Greek letter. ~ MU
A22. What does a clinging vine often develop into? ~ TYRANT
A24. Who are the really free people in the "Land of the Free"? ~ TRAMPS
A25. What two letters pronounced together make a word which means the dwelling place of an American Indian? ~ TP
A26. What kind of glance does the movie villain employ? ~ LEER
A28. What was always running around the castles in Ye Goode Olde Days? ~ MOAT
A29. What suffix is often used to form a plural? ~ ES
A30. What suffix is often used to form feminine nouns? ~ ESS
A32. What must you do to be a good observer? ~ SEE
A33. What is a necessary ingredient of a golden fizz? ~ EGG
A34. How is "oil" pronounced east of the Bowery? ~ ERL
A35. What terrifying sound is heard in the African jungle? ~ ROAR
A37. The scoria from a volcano (Plural—Note: The only place it is proper to form the plural of this noun by adding "s" is in this puzzle—otherwise it wouldn't come out right.) ~ SLAGS
A39. What is the language of the Celts in the Highlands of Scotland? ~ ERSE
A40. What King of Bashan is only heard of nowadays in crossword puzzles? (We'll help you out, the second letter is G). ~ OG
A41. What do bad radio announcers get? ~ AIR
A42. What word means "every one of any number considered separately"? (abbr.) ~ EA
A43. What are strawberries in Alaska? ~ RARE
A46. What is "a little shoot"? ~ SPRIG
A48. What is often told by married men? ~ TALE
A52. In what state is Mobile? (abbr.) ~ ALA
A53. What is a pet name for your father's daughter? ~ SIS
A54. What do girls become after visiting Horizontal 6? ~ MRS
A56. What can be seen from the shore of the Ægean? ~ SEA
A57. In what continent is Alberta? (abbr.) ~ NA
A58. What was Man-of-War's mother? ~ MARE
A59. What is another name for a plot? ~ SITE
A61. Name a French unit of weight (abbr.). ~ GR
A62. What part of the pie would the kids like? ~ ENTIRE
A64. What is every "live one?" ~ MORTAL
A65. What is half a measure of type? ~ EN
A66. What letters after a man's name indicates that he "works to beat hell"? ~ DD
A67. Who was Goddess of the Dawn? ~ EOS
A69. What river was made famous by the crosswords? ~ PO
A70. Name a French definite article. ~ LE
A71. What did Jennie Lind do at Niagara Falls? ~ SANG
A73. What drug is made from a tropical plant? ~ ALOES
A75. What is a stupid fellow? ~ DOLT
A77. What does the successful husband do to keep peace in the family? ~ HEEDS
A78. What slang word means suspicious; wary? ~ LEERY

D1. Who tried to vamp Ulysses on the Island of Ogygia? ~ CALYPSO
D2. What is the name of the sloth which inhabits crossword puzzles? ~ AI
D3. What does a young man with taking ways have to stand—if he's caught? ~ TRIAL
D4. If money makes the mare go—what makes her stop? ~ HO
D5. What rode the nightmare in our childhood days? ~ OGRE
D6. Name a necessary article in our language. ~ AN
D7. What is a bottle of pre-war Scotch to any "Here's How!" owner? ~ TREAT
D8. Name one of the several words implying consent. ~ AY
D9. What do little children play in? ~ ROMPERS
D10. What is that which comes last? ~ LATTER
D12. What is the briefest way to abbreviate Receiving Office? ~ RO
D13. Name a preposition of place. ~ AT
D15. What is a wrestling match? ~ TUSSLE
D18. Name more than one unit. ~ ONES
D20. What do ham actors usually do? ~ BRAG
D23. Name a river in England that runs into the North Sea. ~ TEES
D24. What do golfers play golf in? ~ TOGS
D27. What do youths convalescing from love sickness often have? ~ RELAPSE
D28. What do you have when your spirits are low? ~ MEGRIMS
D31. In what continent is Bolivia? (abbr.) ~ SA
D34. What suffix is used to form the comparative degree? ~ ER
D36. Where do little fish come from? ~ ROE
D38. What does a fresh young man get who is too bree: y with his girl? ~ AIR
D39. What would you do at a filling station? ~ EAT
D43. What are queens to the Hindoos? ~ RANEES
D44. Name an Irish term of endearment. ~ ALANNAH
D45. Name one of the Crossword Puzzle Gods. ~ RA
D46. What is a more respectful name for the old man? ~ SIRE
D47. Name an adjective meaning fierte; stern. ~ GRIM
D49. Name a little word used to express similarity. ~ AS
D50. How must every lawyer do his business? ~ LEGALLY
D51. What is the small e r of a plant called? ~ EARLET
D53. What is the name of a variety of carnelian used as a gem? ~ SARD
D55. What sign do many speedy motorists fail to heed? ~ STOP
D58. Name a small insect. ~ MIDGE
D60. Name a verb which means "to gnaw off; to corrode." ~ ERODE
D63. What is the mo t famous thing about Pittsburgh? ~ SOOT
D67. Give a Spanish definite article. ~ EL
D68. In what direction from New York is Bermuda? ~ SE
D72. In what direction from New York is Portland, Maine? ~ NE
D73. What is the proper answer to Question 49 Vertical? ~ AS
D74. What is an abbreviation for Solicitor at Law? ~ SL
D76. What is the well known companion of "either"? ~ OR


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
D38: What does a fresh young man get who is too bree: y with his girl? → breezy
D51: What is the small e r of a plant called? → ear
D63: What is the mo t famous thing about Pittsburgh? → most

